cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AtmosphericDispersion.jl
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Paul-Adrian
    family-names: Gogîță
    affiliation: Faculty of Physics, University of Bucharest
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/AtmosphericDispersion.jl
abstract: >-
  Gaussian-plume atmospheric dispersion of stack releases: dilution factor,
  time-integrated air concentration, dry and wet ground deposition, and
  resuspension, over Pasquill-Gifford stability classes and a wind rose. The
  solver is nuclide-agnostic; tritium release from a CANDU stack is a
  parameterisation of it. Developed from a 2021 BSc thesis at the Faculty of
  Physics, University of Bucharest.
keywords:
  - atmospheric dispersion
  - Gaussian plume
  - radiological assessment
  - Briggs plume rise
  - Pasquill-Gifford
  - Julia
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-24
